# Shopify SEO content

Owner: Marketing Bot. SEO titles, meta descriptions, alt text, blog posts, on request or when the coach suggests it after unlock. Honest, specific copy, one approved batch at a time (max 10 products). Plugin rules apply; needs write_products, write_files, write_content.

Keywords: start from the merchant's words, the product and the customer; check real searches with web search. Never invent volumes or rankings. One main phrase per page, written for people. No stuffing, no copying competitors.

## Product and collection SEO

1. `get-product` (`id`) or `get-collection`; note title, description, handle.
2. Propose before and after: SEO title 60 characters max (main phrase first, brand last); meta description 155 characters max (what, who, one reason to click). Never change a live product's handle.
3. On yes, `graphql_mutation`:
```graphql
mutation UpdateProductSeo($product: ProductUpdateInput!) {
  productUpdate(product: $product) { product { id title seo { title description } } userErrors { field message } }
}
```
Variables: `{ "product": { "id": "gid://shopify/Product/...", "seo": { "title": "...", "description": "..." } } }`
```graphql
mutation UpdateCollectionSeo($collection: CollectionUpdateInput!) {
  collectionUpdate(collection: $collection) { collection { id title seo { title description } } userErrors { field message } }
}
```
Variables: `{ "collection": { "id": "gid://shopify/Collection/...", "seo": { "title": "...", "description": "..." } } }`

2026-01 fallback, if `CollectionUpdateInput` / `collection:` is unknown, retry once with:
```graphql
mutation UpdateCollectionSeo($input: CollectionInput!) {
  collectionUpdate(input: $input) { collection { id title seo { title description } } userErrors { field message } }
}
```
Variables: `{ "input": { "id": "gid://shopify/Collection/...", "seo": { "title": "...", "description": "..." } } }`
4. Re-read and confirm.

## Image alt text

Plain description (product, color, use), 125 characters max. Media ids from ProductForCreative (`shopify-short-form-video`). On yes:
```graphql
mutation UpdateImageAlt($files: [FileUpdateInput!]!) {
  fileUpdate(files: $files) { files { id alt } userErrors { field message } }
}
```
Variables: `{ "files": [{ "id": "gid://shopify/MediaImage/...", "alt": "..." }] }`

## Blog posts

1. Find the blog:
```graphql
query Blogs {
  blogs(first: 5) { nodes { id title handle } }
}
```
2. One topic answering a real customer question tied to a product. Outline (title, 3 to 5 headings, where products appear); get a yes.
3. Draft 600 to 900 words in the merchant's voice, linking 1 to 3 products. No invented stats, quotes or claims.
4. On yes, create as a draft:
```graphql
mutation CreateArticle($article: ArticleCreateInput!) {
  articleCreate(article: $article) { article { id title handle isPublished } userErrors { field message } }
}
```
Variables: `{ "article": { "blogId": "gid://shopify/Blog/...", "title": "...", "author": { "name": "<store name>" }, "body": "<p>...</p>", "summary": "<p>...</p>", "tags": ["..."], "isPublished": false } }`
5. Paste the admin link. Publishing is the merchant's call.
